From: TuNaiChao <tunaichao@uniontech.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: Fix Ruby tests for modern minitest and skip flaky cases

Old minitest 4 API is gone in minitest 5: the MiniTest constant is now
Minitest, MiniTest::Unit::AssertionFailedError is Minitest::Assertion,
assert_not_equal is refute_equal, and plain `require "minitest"` no
longer registers the at_exit runner, so tests would silently run zero
cases. Rename accordingly and require minitest/autorun.
Constant rename based on upstream commit 50359a3b.

Also skip two suites whose reliability depends on the build machine:
- test_typing.rb entirely: typing through a live X server depends on
  window focus, keymap state and no input-method interference, and is
  inherently flaky on shared/CI machines (upstream already marks 5 of
  the 14 cases known-broken; observed empty and IME-mangled output on
  aarch64 workers and desktops alike);
- test_mousemove_same_position_of_the_other_window when a window
  manager is running: windowmove --sync intermittently exits 1 when
  the WM is slow.

